diff --git a/docs/src/man/man1/halcmd.1.adoc b/docs/src/man/man1/halcmd.1.adoc
index 6c6b19b528..4d010eeca1 100644
--- a/docs/src/man/man1/halcmd.1.adoc
+++ b/docs/src/man/man1/halcmd.1.adoc
@@ -300,6 +300,28 @@ variable substitution take place.
 
 === Environment Variables
 
+*HAL_RTMOD_PATH* is the complete ordered, colon-separated search path used by
+*loadrt*.  The first regular file named `<component><module-extension>` wins.
+When it is unset, the compiled standard realtime module directory is used.
+An explicitly empty value, relative directory, empty element, or directory not
+compiled into LinuxCNC's trust set is rejected in full.  A selected file that
+fails to load is reported without trying a later copy.  The protected *rtapi*
+and *hal_lib* modules are always loaded from the standard directory.
+
+Additional trusted directories are selected at build time with
+`./configure --with-extra-rtlib-dirs=DIR[:DIR...]`; every entry must be
+absolute.  For example, a build trusting `/opt/integrator/rtlib` may use:
+
+----
+HAL_RTMOD_PATH=/opt/integrator/rtlib:/usr/lib/linuxcnc/modules
+----
+
+*HAL_RTMOD_DIR* remains available as the standard single realtime module
+directory for compatibility.  *linuxcnc* and *halrun* preserve a caller's
+*HAL_RTMOD_PATH*, otherwise they initialize it to that standard directory.
+The userspace realtime master captures the path at startup, so restart the
+realtime session after changing it.
+
 Environment variables have the following formats:
 
 - *$ENVVAR* followed by end-of-line or whitespace
